# (d) Claude calls compact_after_turn while replying: the mod compacts about 1 s after the reply ends.
title:   Compacting on request, right after the turn
caption: You can ask Claude to compact without waiting. Claude passes the request to idle-compact, which lets the current reply finish, waits one second, then compacts: no 20-minute wait and no size check.
note:    1 column = a quarter of a second. The one-second wait lets the reply settle before Claude Code compacts.
focus:   C
term:    Turn — one round of the conversation: your message, and everything Claude does until its reply is done.
term:    compact_after_turn — the tool idle-compact gives Claude for this. You just say "compact after this turn".

time                       0   1s  2s
claude      -S~~~~~~~~~~~~~E-----------
request     ------t--------------------
wait                       [===F
compaction  --------------------C------

legend
S  message sent — you ask, Claude starts  blue
~  Claude working  teal
t  compact requested — Claude uses compact_after_turn  teal
E  reply done  teal
=  1 s wait  violet
F  wait over — 1 second later  violet
C  compacted — now a short summary  green
